    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/en/">VeVolt</a><span>/</span><a href="/en/blog/">Blog</a></nav>
    <div class="article-intro"><div class="article-hero"><img src="/assets/blog/recarga-condominio.webp" width="1280" height="720" alt="VeVolt Condo app displays a shared EV charger booking schedule" fetchpriority="high"></div><header class="article-header"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="signal"></span>VeVolt guide</p><h1>App to book an EV charger in a condominium</h1><p class="lede">A booking app replaces scattered messages with one view of residents, chargers and time slots. It organizes access to the schedule without connecting to or controlling the electrical equipment.</p><p class="article-meta">Updated 03/08/2026 · 2 min read</p></header></div>
    <div class="article-layout"><div class="article-body"><section><h2>Choose a workflow, not just a calendar</h2><p>Useful booking connects the participant, charger, start and end time, completed session and manual record. This gives property managers context for the monthly close.</p></section><section><h2>How VeVolt Condo booking works</h2><p>The administrator creates a hub, adds up to 10 chargers and invites up to 50 participants. Residents book available time slots and enter consumption and cost after use.</p><ul><li>Private hub</li><li>Resident invitations</li><li>Conflict-free time slots</li><li>Manual session records</li><li>Monthly closing support</li></ul></section><section><h2>Know the product boundaries</h2><p>VeVolt does not use OCPP, start charging, meter energy, bill residents or balance electrical load. Eligible new customers can try the monthly Condo plan free for 15 days on Google Play.</p></section><nav class="article-context-links" aria-label="Continue the condominium charging guide"><h2>Continue the condominium charging guide</h2><ul><li><a href="/en/condo">Try VeVolt Condo</a></li><li><a href="/en/blog/electric-car-charger-in-condominium">Read the complete condominium guide</a></li><li><a href="/en/blog/shared-ev-charger-condominium-rules">Define shared charger rules</a></li></ul></nav><section><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><details class="faq-item"><summary>Does the app work as a charger remote?</summary><p>No. It organizes bookings and records only.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Do invited residents pay for Premium?</summary><p>No. They join the Condo hub without Premium.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Is the monthly plan available with a trial?</summary><p>Eligible new customers can receive a 15-day trial through Google Play.</p></details></div></section></div>
    <aside class="article-aside"><h2>Organize with VeVolt Condo</h2><p>Organize residents, schedules, sessions and manual cost allocation with VeVolt Condo. Eligible new customers can try the monthly plan free for 15 days on Google Play.</p><a class="play-badge-link" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=br.com.vevolt" rel="noopener" aria-label="Get it on Google Play"><img src="/assets/google-play-badge-en.png" width="564" height="168" alt="Get it on Google Play"></a><h2>Sources and further reading</h2><ul class="source-list"><li><a href="https://www.gov.br/aneel/pt-br/assuntos/veiculos-eletricos" rel="noopener noreferrer">ANEEL - Electric vehicles and charging rules</a></li><li><a href="https://www.agenciasp.sp.gov.br/governo-de-sp-sanciona-lei-que-permite-instalacao-de-carregadores-de-carros-eletricos-em-condominios/" rel="noopener noreferrer">São Paulo State Government - Charging in condominiums</a></li></ul></aside></div>
    <section class="section compact"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="kicker">Related guides</p><h2>Keep learning</h2></div></div><div class="grid two"><article class="article-card"><div class="article-card-body"><h3>EV charging station near me: how to find and verify one</h3><p>Learn how to find nearby EV chargers and check connector, power, access, price and recent conditions before leaving.</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/blog/ev-charging-station-near-me">Read article →</a></div></article><article class="article-card"><div class="article-card-body"><h3>Electric-car connectors: Type 2, CCS2, CHAdeMO and GB/T</h3><p>Identify common EV charging connectors and verify compatibility before choosing a charging station.</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/blog/electric-car-connectors-type-2-ccs2-chademo-gbt">Read article →</a></div></article></div></section>
